new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9a93083
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SUMMARY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+# Summary
+
+## Changed
+- `stockreport/report.py`: `render(items, "markdown")` now builds a table with the vendored `tabulate` using `style="pipe"` and `number_format=".2f"`. A blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>` follow the table. The columns, their order and the sort are the same as in the text report. Literal `|` characters in item names are escaped as `\|` so they don't break the table.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` now accepts `markdown`.
+- `README.md`: documented the new option.
+- No tests were added or changed. The existing `tests/test_report.py` already covers the exact output.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest` ran 3 tests, all OK. These include `test_markdown_output` and `test_cli_markdown`, which compares the exact output of `python -m stockreport inventory.csv --format markdown`.
+
+## Not verified
+- The `|` escaping has no test. I didn't run a case with a pipe in a name, and the escaped text will make that column wider.
+- I did not check how GitHub renders the output. I only compared it with the expected string in the test.
+- I did not change `vendor/`, add dependencies, or touch any file outside the allowed list.
